From 1614cc94c74727c6768aba696ea8588c81a51aa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:29:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] FixedPointSolver: adaptive tolerance of the NewtonK0 method

The option AdaptiveLinearSolverTolerance (Eisenstat and Walker) applies to
the iterative solver of the tangent operator of the NewtonK0 method, whose
tolerance given by TangentLinearSolver is restored at the end of each
resolution; it is refused with the other methods. On the cube of the
test, 36 iterations of the conjugate gradient instead of 118 to 135, 12
Newton iterations instead of 8.

The norm of the residual of the linear solves (first choice of Eisenstat
and Walker) is added to the iterations information (ResidualNorm), in the
Newton solver and in the fixed point solver, and checked by the test: the
mutation which does not compute it is now detected, as the ones which do
not set the tolerance, do not restore it or do not refuse it.
